pull_request.body:
This PR takes only the review changes that look clearly corrective rather than theory-design choices.

Article changes:
- soften the historical Naur claim from an exclusive inference to a crucial-premise reading;
- explain how the article's four implementation roles relate to the proposal-selection and residue decompositions;
- narrow the Commonplace episode from observational causal support to documented retained-state consumption, theory-state revision, and later reuse consistent with mediation;
- replace the "loop has no outside" / ship-of-Theseus rhetoric with the narrower claim that no component inside the declared revision surface is exempt by position;
- keep the current latest-main additions about the article being a program rather than results and the workspace-optimization comparison.

The accompanying workshop report deliberately leaves the deeper residuum unresolved: the minimum operational threshold for theory, a possible H1–H5 hypothesis ladder, stronger synthetic controls for the theory intervention, canonical mapping among decompositions, decomposition of global fit, operational scaling metrics, production-time instrumentation, program/Bitter-Lesson article overlap, and the stability boundary of a reflective loop.

The intent is to make the obvious precision fixes now while preserving the deeper questions as research work rather than settling them by editorial fiat.
